 ### Local Planar Alignment of 3DGS
-This subtopic describes enforcing Gaussian centers to lie on object surfaces by projecting them onto local tangent planes computed from KNN covariance matrices. It sets itself apart by providing a geometric constraint that aligns Gaussians with surfaces, improving mesh quality [S1]. Choose this when you need to extract cleaner meshes from 3DGS [S1]. Link: [Local Planar Alignment](15766-appearance-and-physical-modeling.md).
